# Paths .github/workflows/semgrep.yml does not scan, each a confirmed
# false positive. This file replaces Semgrep's default ignore list; the
# scan still covers only files tracked by git, so installed and built
# output (node_modules/, vendor/, .nuxt/, dist/) is never a target.

# Mirrors Furo's own upstream footer template (see the file's own header
# comment) — Sphinx renders this into static HTML at build time, with no
# request handling involved. next.link/prev.link/path/icon_dict.url are
# Sphinx's own navigation values, never request-controlled input, so the
# var-in-href rule's XSS concern doesn't apply here.
docs/_templates/page.html

# Credentials::NOBODY is a bcrypt hash of nothing anyone types, verified
# when no user matches the e-mail so a failed sign-in takes the same time
# whether the account exists or not. It guards no account and is not a
# credential; the generic bcrypt-hash rule can't tell that from a leaked
# one by its shape.
demo/backend/src/Auth/Credentials.php

# The end-to-end test that a Markdown reply renders safely: the <script>
